d potentially price  rises as a consequence in time i think  we can fill the gap but short term i  think we need to maybe relax the visa  rule so we can get some of the eu  drivers back into the uk  long term we'll be fine we just need to  build up to it  [Music]  labor costs are already going up  well we expect to get another  array a wage wage increase imminently  you know our second third in some cases  this year now uh you circle of 10 i  guess as companies struggle to meet  demand drivers have been offered pay  rises in order to ensure they stay in  the profession  and major employers like tesco amazon  and john lewis have offered four-figure  signing on bonuses to new drivers  inducing drivers  football style signing on fees  retention bonuses payable after three  months i've heard numbers up to five  thousand pounds pension  and while hgv drivers are a problem for  everyone there are labour shortages in  other industries too  the confederation of british industries  says there's demand for butchers meat  processors fruit and flower pickers  warehouse workers cleaners chefs  scaffolders carpenters welders  electrical engineers and factory  assembly workers  there are many roles and career  opportunities for local people here but  we simply don't have the people coming  forward for the for the jobs meanwhile  there was still up to 1.6 million people  on furlough at the end of july and the  government hopes that when the scheme  ends this month those made redundant may  fill these roles the cbi is skeptical  the firms that have still got people on  furlough they've been paying for those  so they must be doing so in the belief  that they're going to need those workers  uh pretty soon otherwise they wouldn't  have held on to them and of course  they're going to be some dislocation the  people on that furlough scheme right now  won't necessarily have the skills to  slot straight into these vacancies  [Music]  a shortage of semiconductors the  material from which microchips are made  has hit industries from consumer  electronics to car production initially  the pandemic closed factories in  southeast asia where most semiconductors  are produced then a surge in demand from  people working from home saw them  scramble to meet orders  when the car market recovered faster  than expected chip suppliers couldn't  keep pace  demand is also causing shortages of the  raw materials for the building trade  cement concrete steel stone and timber  prices are rising as a consequence it is  causing product shortages on shelf and  my concern is that this will only get  worse because we're now in september and  we're coming into the critical time of  year where we start to stock build for  christmas  which is obviously a really important  time of year for everyone the cbi warns  that labour shortages could last two  years as employers retrain and hire a  domestic workforce  and some analysts believe that  post-brexit there could be a permanent  impact with reduced supply of goods and  higher prices  [Music]

